<html>
    <head>
        <title>TOSS predictions</title>
        <style type="text/css" media="all">@import "/toss_designs/design.css";</style>
        
    </head>
    <body>
        <a name='results'></a>
        <h1>TOSS predictions</h1>
        <p>
        Note: If you need help interpreting this result table, see information below prediction table or click <a href='#doc'>here</a>.
        </p>
        <TMPL_IF name='TOSS_LIST'>
            <form name = 'edit' method='post'>
                <input type='hidden' name='page' value = 'toss_details'>
                <input type='hidden' name='pred_nbr' value = ''>
                <input type='hidden' name='gene_name' value = '<TMPL_VAR name="GENE_NAME">'>
                <input type='hidden' name='rna_seq' value = ''>
                <input type='hidden' name='5ss_dist' value = ''>
                <input type='hidden' name='inhouse_criteria_str' value = ''>
                <input type='hidden' name='offtarget_major' value = ''>
                <input type='hidden' name='offtarget_minor' value = ''>
                <input type='hidden' name='ess_mapping' value = ''>
                <input type='hidden' name='mapped_seq' value = ''>
                <table border=1>
                    <tr class='header'>
                        <td>Nbr</td>
                        <td>TOSS Sequence (tail-antisens)</td>
                        <td >ESS / ESE Mapping</td>
                        <td>Target gene</td>
                        <td>In silico offtargets</td>
                        <td >Binding region (identified in red)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <TMPL_LOOP name = 'TOSS_LIST'>
                        <tr>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="NBR"></td>
                            <td>UAUGAUAGGGACUUAGGGUG<b>-</b><TMPL_VAR name="RNA_SEQUENCE"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="ESS_MAPPING"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="PERFECT_TARGETS"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="OFFTARGETS_MAJOR"></td>
                            <td><pre><font face="courier new"><TMPL_VAR name="MAPPED_SEQUENCE"></font></pre></td>
                        </tr>
                    </TMPL_LOOP>
                </table>
                <br />
            </form>
            <p>
                <a name='doc'></a>
                Following is a description of each column presented in the TOSS design table above:
                <ul>
                <li class="leaf" >
                    <b>Nbr:</b> The prediction number. Please note that the designs are sorted by order of preference based on the following 4 criterias listed below:
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            1. TOSS optimal distance score. TOSS that are within 30 nucleotides upstream of the 3&prime; end of the submitted 
                            sequence are listed first. We consider this criteria as most important if the the goal is to inhibit the 5&prime;ss 
                            or 3&prime;ss that is located at the 3&prime; end of the AIR. Please re-assess the order if the goal is to repress 
                            the upstream splice site at the 5&prime; end of the AIR. 
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            2. Number of possible off-targets with four mismatches or less. The designs with the least number of off-targets 
                            are listed first.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            3. ESS / ESE mapping score. TOSS overlapping ESE are favored because they might provide further inhibition 
                            by antagonizing the binding of positive splicing regulators. For more information about ESS / ESE mapping, 
                            please refer to the description below.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            4. TOSS distance. TOSS designs that are located upstream of 30 nucleotides from the 3&prime; end of AIR, are ranked by 
                            distance relative to the 3&prime; end of AIR.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li class="leaf"  >
                    <b>TOSS Sequence (tail-antisens):</b> The TOSS sequence is shown 5&prime; to 3&prime; and include the hnRNP A1 recruting tail. 
                    The sequence of the tail sequence is followed by a "-" sign and then the antisense portion.
                </li>
                <li class="leaf" >
                    <b>ESS / ESE Mapping:</b> 
                    In order to provide the user with information concerning the existence of putative exonic silencer sequences (ESS) 
                    and exonic enhancer sequences (ESE),  we have included a search for these elements based on the following studies: 
                    <ul>
                    <li>
                    Cartegni L, Wang J, Zhu Z, Zhang MQ, Krainer AR. ESEfinder: A web resource to identify exonic splicing enhancers. 
                    Nucleic Acids Res. 2003 Jul 1;31(13):3568-71. PubMed PMID: <a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/?term=12824367">12824367</a>; 
                    PubMed Central PMCID: <a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC169022/">PMC169022</a>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                    Stadler MB, Shomron N, Yeo GW, Schneider A, Xiao X, Burge CB. Inference of splicing regulatory activities by sequence neighborhood analysis. 
                    PLoS Genet. 2006 Nov 24;2(11):e191. Epub 2006 Sep 28. PubMed PMID: 
                    <a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/?term=17121466">17121466</a>; 
                    PubMed Central PMCID: <a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1657047/">PMC1657047</a>.
                    </li>
                    </ul>
                    Each ESE and each ESS motifs are searched in the submitted sequence. If an ESE or an ESS is found, each 
                    nucleotide position in the corresponding site in the submitted sequence is attributed a +1 or -1 score, respectively. 
                    The values shown in the column represents the sum of these scores for each position of the antisense region. 
                    For example, an ESE / ESS mapping of "<font color="red">-3-2-2-1-1-1-1-1</font>00-1-1<font color="blue">14566532</font>" 
                    means that the 5&prime; portion of the binding region is overrepresented by ESSs (in red) whereas the 3&prime; region is 
                    overrepresented by ESEs (in blue). Note that a TOSS design targeting a region enriched in ESE motifs should be favored.
                </li>
                <li class="leaf" >
                    <b>Target gene:</b> This column shows targets with perfect match ("|") to antisense region of TOSS designs.
                </li>
                <li class="leaf" >
                    <b>In silico offtargets:</b> This column shows possible off-targets with 4 mismatches (".") or less relative to 
                    the antisense portion of TOSS.
                </li>
                <li class="leaf" >
                    <b>Binding region:</b> The submitted region is shown, with the portion complementary to the TOSS indicated in red.</li>
                </ul>
                <br/>
                Go <a href='#results'>back</a> to result table.
            </p>
        <TMPL_ELSE>
            No valid TOSS could be generated using this AIR sequence.
        </TMPL_IF>
    </body>
</html>
